  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "new-task-read-gates",
      "finding": "NewTaskDialog remains mounted with creating initially false, while all existing reads remain gated by open. The new useTaskProfileChoices maps the already loaded AgentProfilesView and translations; it does not fetch, use SWR, call server actions, or run an effect. Its onManage opens settings only when invoked. NewTask itself is rendered only under open &&. Creating a React element for notices/keyDialogNode does not itself mount that component.",
      "witnesses": [
        "components/workspace/issue-workspace.tsx:326,593",
        "components/coordinator/new-task-dialog.tsx:89,96,101-104,115,176-198",
        "components/coordinator/task-profile-picker.tsx:77-95",
        "components/settings/factory-profiles-data.ts:62-67"
      ],
      "equality": "factory-profiles-data.ts is byte-identical at both source commits; the NewTask diff preserves all read gates."
    },
    {
      "id": "closed-neighbour-slots",
      "finding": "The adjacent new-bot slot is open-only. Search starts with searchOpen=false and usePresence(false).value=null; IssueWorkspace mounts GlobalSearch only when search.value is truthy. The refactored search data hook still calls the same useSiteSearch(query, workspaceId); no new initial-workspace search mount is introduced. Settings content is created as JSX but rendered only in the settingsShown branch; new members/audit screens do not thereby mount on the ordinary conversation startup path.",
      "witnesses": [
        "components/nav/new-bot-dialog.tsx:59-61",
        "components/workspace/issue-workspace.tsx:236,328-329,598-602,633-644",
        "lib/use-presence.ts:10-19",
        "components/nav/global-search.tsx:92-105",
        "components/settings/settings-view.tsx:97-116,144-145"
      ],
      "limit": "Once Search is opened, a private SearchPalette may remain mounted during its exit presence; this review does not characterize private slot effects."
    },
    {
      "id": "frame-panel-ownership",
      "finding": "FRAME_OWNS_PANEL=true changes actual mount ownership for the ordinary coordinator conversation. IssueWorkspace forms overview/context and browser React elements in panels.tabs, passes them through ConversationPanels.Provider, and suppresses the old side BrowserPane, ContextPanel and Sheet via !panelsInFrame. Thus there is no unconditional double-render of the old and new panel paths. Whether and when the supplied tab content actually mounts is determined by the private ThreadScreen. The public adapter alone cannot prove request equivalence, lower SQL counts, or hidden-tab unmounting.",
      "witnesses": [
        "components/workspace/issue-workspace.tsx:548,576-586,651,659,664,673",
        "components/coordinator/conversation-panels.tsx:1-11",
        "components/coordinator/coordinator-chat.tsx:478-480,552"
      ],
      "defaults": "Public default FRAME_OWNS_PANEL=false, FRAME_OWNS_HEADER=false, ThreadScreen=null. These defaults do not prove the official hosted UI behavior.",
      "detail": "BrowserPane's only diff adds inTab and changes its root wrapper from ResizablePane to section when true; its existing hooks are unchanged. ContextPanel is not changed by this main diff."
    },
    {
      "id": "header-address-and-compact-chat",
      "finding": "FRAME_OWNS_HEADER=true adds a redirect only when threadsView is present: it removes the legacy threads query and, with no threadId, selects tasks. This can alter a legacy bookmarked startup route; it is not an unconditional ordinary /mikka redirect. CoordinatorChat now allows a non-null ThreadScreen for compact chats too, while embedded chats retain the old path; compact screens receive panels=undefined. Normal noncompact chats already used a non-null ThreadScreen before this change.",
      "witnesses": [
        "components/workspace/issue-workspace.tsx:258-263,642-649",
        "components/coordinator/coordinator-chat.tsx:476-480,552"
      ],
      "limit": "Actual UI renderer mounting/layout must be evaluated with the selected overlay; public JSX objects are not evidence that supplied children have mounted."
    },
    {
